<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Soldiers'_Monument_(Santa_Fe,_New_Mexico)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Soldiers' Monument is a controversial memorial monument at the center of the Santa Fe Plaza. It was erected as a 33 feet (10 m) stone cenotaph, consisting of an obelisk and a plinth during 1867–1868. During the late nineteenth century, the monument was used for annual Memorial Day events, a place for Union veterans to gather, decorate the cenotaph, and hear brief presentations."@en .
