<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Grand_Bazaar,_Istanbul> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Grand Bazaar** (Template:Lang-tr, meaning ‘Covered Market’; also *Büyük Çarşı*, meaning ‘Grand Market’) in [Istanbul](:Istanbul) is one of the largest and oldest [covered markets](:Bazaar) in the world, with 61 covered streets and over 4,000 shops on a total area of 30,700 m2, attracting between 250,000 and 400,000 visitors daily. In 2014, it was listed No.1 among the world's most-visited tourist attractions with 91,250,000 annual visitors. The Grand Bazaar at [Istanbul](:Istanbul) is often regarded as one of the first [shopping malls](:Shopping_malls) of the [world](:World)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
