<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Shrine_of_Baha'al-Halim> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Shrine of Baha'al-Halim** (Template:Lang-ur is the shrine of Baha'al-Halim, an Islamic saint. It is the earliest of three located in [Uch](:Uch) in present-day [Punjab](:Punjab%2C_Pakistan), [Pakistan](:Pakistan). It is one of the five monuments in [Uch Sharif](:Uch), [Pakistan](:Pakistan) which are on the tentative list of the [UNESCO](:UNESCO) [World Heritage Sites](:World_Heritage_Sites).The octagonal tomb is built of glazed bricks with turrets at each of its eight corners. A single dome is above a smaller octagonal dome with arched windows that sits on the base."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
