<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sytin's_house_in_Sytinsky_lane> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Sytin's house in Sytinsky lane (Russian: Дом Сытина в Сытинском переулке) is a wooden building in the center of Moscow (Sytinsky lane, house 5, building 5). A unique example of the construction of the city before the fire of 1812, it is the main house of the city manor of the noble family Sytinykh. The house was built in 1804 in the classicism style. It has the status of an object of cultural heritage of federal significance."@en .
