<http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_African_War_Memorial_(Toronto)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The South African War Memorial is a memorial located at University Avenue and Queen Street West in Toronto, Ontario, Canada. Commissioned in 1910, largely as the result of the efforts of James Mason, and designed by Walter Seymour Allward to commemorate Canada's participation in the Boer War, it consists of three bronze figures at the base of a granite column. Another bronze figure is found at the top of the memorial. It was restored in 2001. \n* Winged figure holding a golden crown at the top of the obelisk. \n* The base of Walter Seymour Allward's South African War Memorial in the winter. \n*"@en .
