<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Douglas_Tilden> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Douglas Tilden (May 1, 1860 to August 5, 1935) was an American sculptor. He was deaf from a bout of scarlet fever at the age of four and attended the California School for the Deaf in Berkeley, California (now in Fremont, California). He sculpted many statues that are located today throughout San Francisco, Berkeley, and the San Francisco Bay Area."@en .
