<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lone_Cedar_Tree> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Lone Cedar Tree** is a historical monument located on 600 East between 300 and 400 South, near downtown [Salt Lake City](:Salt_Lake_City), [Utah](:Utah), [United States](:United_States). According to [Mormon Pioneers](:Mormon_Pioneers), it was the location of the only tree growing in the valley in 1847, when they arrived. On July 4, 1933, the [Daughters of Utah Pioneers](:Daughters_of_Utah_Pioneers) erected the monument to honor the Mormon heritage and history of Salt Lake City."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
