<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pushkinskaya_Street_(Rostov-on-Don)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Pushkinskaya Street (Russian: Пушкинская улица) is one of the main streets in Rostov-on-Don. The street is named after the Russian poet Alexander Pushkin. Many old houses, university buildings and the Don State Public Library are located on this street. The Pushkinskaya Street is a green boulevard, it goes parallel to the Don River."@en .
