<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Illinois_Freedom_Bell> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Illinois Freedom Bell** is located in [Mount Morris, Illinois](:Mount_Morris%2C_Illinois), United States, and is the official freedom bell of the U.S. state of [Illinois](:Illinois). The bell was created for a church in [Lake Geneva](:Lake_Geneva%2C_Wisconsin), [Wisconsin](:Wisconsin) as a replica of the [Liberty Bell](:Liberty_Bell) in 1862. In 1910, while it was being moved across the frozen [Geneva Lake](:Geneva_Lake) following a fire at the church, the ice cracked and the bell sank to the bottom of the lake. It was [salvaged](:Marine_salvage) in 1960 and the village of Mount Morris acquired it in 1966. The Illinois Freedom Bell is rung during the annual Let Freedom Ring festival, and it can be found beneath a [gazebo](:Gazebo) on the village square. The bell has been credited with starting an [Independence Day](:Independence_Day_%28United_States%29) bell-ringing tradition across the United States. The bell was designated the official Illinois Freedom Bell in 1971."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
