<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mexico_City> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Mexico City** (Template:Lang-es, Template:IPA-es; abbr.: **CDMX**; [Nahuatl](:Nahuatl): *Altepetl Mexico*) is the [capital](:Capital_city) and [largest city](:Primate_city) of [Mexico](:Mexico), and the [most populous city](:List_of_North_American_cities_by_population) in [North America](:North_America). One of the world's [alpha cities](:Globalization_and_World_Cities_Research_Network), it is located in the [Valley of Mexico](:Valley_of_Mexico) within the high Mexican central [plateau](:Plateau), at an altitude of 2,240 meters (7,350 ft). The city has 16 [boroughs or *demarcaciones territoriales*](:Boroughs_of_Mexico_City), which are in turn divided into [neighborhoods or *colonias*](:List_of_neighborhoods_in_Mexico_City).The 2020 population for the [city proper](:City_proper) was 9,209,944, with a land area of 1,495 square kilometers (577 sq mi). According to the most recent definition agreed upon by the federal and state governments, the population of [Greater Mexico City](:Greater_Mexico_City) is 21,804,515, which makes it the [sixth-largest metropolitan area](:List_of_largest_cities%23List) in the world, the second-largest [urban agglomeration](:Urban_area) in the [Western Hemisphere](:Western_Hemisphere) (behind [São Paulo](:S%C3%A3o_Paulo), [Brazil](:Brazil%29), and the largest [Spanish-speaking](:Spanish_language) city (city proper) in the world. [Greater Mexico City](:Greater_Mexico_City) has a [GDP](:Gross_domestic_product) of $411 billion in 2011, which makes it one of the [most productive urban areas in the world](:List_of_cities_by_GDP). The city was responsible for generating 15.8% of Mexico's GDP, and the metropolitan area accounted for about 22% of the country's GDP. If it were an independent country in 2013, Mexico City would be the fifth-largest economy in [Latin America](:Latin_America).Mexico's capital is both the [oldest capital city in the Americas](:List_of_oldest_continuously_inhabited_cities%23America%2C_Middle) and one of two founded by [indigenous people](:Indigenous_peoples_of_the_Americas). The city was originally built on a group of islands in [Lake Texcoco](:Lake_Texcoco) by the [Mexica (Aztecs)](:Mexica) around 1325, under the name [Tenochtitlan](:Tenochtitlan). It was almost completely destroyed in the 1521 [Siege of Tenochtitlan](:Fall_of_Tenochtitlan) and subsequently redesigned and rebuilt in accordance with the [Spanish urban standards](:Spanish_architecture%23Spanish_Colonial_architecture). In 1524, the [municipality](:Municipalities_of_Mexico) of Mexico City was established, known as *México Tenochtitlán*, and as of 1585, it was officially known as *Ciudad de México* (Mexico City). Mexico City was the political, administrative, and financial center of a major part of the [Spanish colonial empire](:Spanish_Empire). After [independence from Spain](:Mexican_War_of_Independence) was achieved, the [federal district](:Federal_district) was created in 1824.After years of demanding greater political [autonomy](:Autonomy), residents were finally given the right to [elect](:Election) both a [head of government](:List_of_mayors_of_Mexico_City) and the representatives of the [unicameral](:Unicameralism) [Legislative Assembly](:Legislative_Assembly_of_Mexico_City) by election in 1997. Ever since, left-wing parties (first the [Party of the Democratic Revolution](:Party_of_the_Democratic_Revolution) and later the [National Regeneration Movement](:National_Regeneration_Movement%29) have controlled both of them. The city has several progressive policies, such as elective [abortions](:Abortion_in_Mexico), a limited form of [euthanasia](:Euthanasia_in_Mexico), [no-fault divorce](:No-fault_divorce), and [same-sex marriage](:Same-sex_marriage_in_Mexico_City). On 29 January 2016, it ceased to be the *Federal District* (Template:Lang-es or *D.F.*) and is now officially known as *Ciudad de México* (or *CDMX*), with a greater degree of autonomy. A clause in the [Constitution of Mexico](:Constitution_of_Mexico), however, prevents it from becoming a state within the Mexican federation, as it is the seat of power in the country, unless the capital of the country were to be relocated elsewhere."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
