<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Conolly's_Folly> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**The Conolly Folly** (Template:Lang-ga, a.k.a. **The Obelisk**, is an obelisk structure located between [Celbridge](:Celbridge), [Leixlip](:Leixlip) and [Maynooth](:Maynooth) in [County Kildare](:County_Kildare), [Ireland](:Ireland). It was built in the mid-18th century by the Conolly family, then owners of the [Castletown Estate](:Castletown_House). It was restored in the mid-20th century by the [Irish Georgian Society](:Irish_Georgian_Society), and is now a [national monument](:National_Monument_%28Ireland%29) in state care."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
