<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Charles_Mulligan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Charles J. Mulligan (September 28, 1866 – March 25, 1916) was an American sculptor. Born in , County Tyrone, Ireland, Mulligan immigrated to America at the age of 17 and found work as a stone cutter in Pullman, Illinois, near Chicago. Mulligan died on March 25, 1916, in Chicago. He died at St. Luke's Hospital accompanied by his wife and three children. At the time of his death, he had just been awarded a commission to build his design of a statue of Mad Anthony Wayne in Fort Wayne, Indiana. He was buried at Mount Greenwood Cemetery."@en .
