<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Douglas_Tilden> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Douglas Tilden** (May 1, 1860 to August 5, 1935) was an American [sculptor](:Sculpture). He was [deaf](:Deafness) from a bout of scarlet fever at the age of four and attended the [California School for the Deaf](:California_School_for_the_Deaf%2C_Fremont) in [Berkeley, California](:Berkeley%2C_California) (now in [Fremont, California](:Fremont%2C_California%29). He sculpted many statues that are located today throughout [San Francisco](:San_Francisco), Berkeley, and the [San Francisco Bay Area](:San_Francisco_Bay_Area)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
