<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Morley_War_Memorial,_Scatcherd_Park> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Morley War Memorial** is a British national [war memorial](:War_memorial) situated in Scatcherd Park, [Morley](:Morley%2C_West_Yorkshire), [Leeds](:Leeds), England. Sculpted by [Walter Henry Gilbert](:Walter_Gilbert_%28sculptor%29) and cast by H. H. Martyn and Co., it was unveiled 21 May 1927 by Alderman Joseph Kirk and accepted by Mayor Alderman Thomas Marshall. The war memorial was added to the [National Heritage List for England](:National_Heritage_List_for_England) on 17 June 1986 as a Grade II listed structure.This memorial commemorates the residents of Morley who were killed in the [First World War](:First_World_War), with 453 names and the [Second World War](:Second_World_War) with 110 names. It was renovated in 2008 and rededicated 29 June the same year."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
