<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tiri_Monastery> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Tiri monastery** ([Georgian](:Georgian_language): თირის მონასტერი, [romanized](:Romanization_of_Georgian): tiris monast'eri) is a 13th-century church near [Tskhinvali](:Tskhinvali) in what is now the disputed territory of [South Ossetia](:South_Ossetia). Built as a [Georgian Orthodox](:Georgian_Orthodox) monastery in a [hall church](:Hall_church) plan, it bears medieval frescoes and Georgian inscriptions. After the 2008 [Russo-Georgian War](:Russo-Georgian_War), the Georgians lost access to the monastery. In 2015, the church building was subjected to maintenance works which infringed on authenticity and partially damaged the frescoes, leading to a controversy in Tskhinvali and protests from Georgia. The monastery is inscribed on the list of Georgia's [Immovable Cultural Monuments of National Significance](:Immovable_Cultural_Monuments_of_National_Significance)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
