<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dover,_Delaware> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Dover** () is the capital and second-largest city of the [U.S. state](:U%2ES%2E_state) of [Delaware](:Delaware). It is also the county seat of [Kent County](:Kent_County%2C_Delaware) and the principal city of the [Dover, DE, Metropolitan Statistical Area](:Kent_County%2C_Delaware), which encompasses all of Kent County and is part of the [Philadelphia](:Philadelphia)–[Wilmington](:Wilmington%2C_Delaware)–[Camden](:Camden%2C_New_Jersey), [PA](:Pennsylvania)–[NJ](:New_Jersey)–DE–[MD](:Maryland), [Combined Statistical Area](:Delaware_Valley). It is located on the [St. Jones River](:St%2E_Jones_River) in the [Delaware River](:Delaware_River) coastal plain. It was named by [William Penn](:William_Penn) for [Dover](:Dover) in [Kent](:Kent), England (for which Kent County is named). As of 2010, the city had a population of 36,047."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
