<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Stanford_Mausoleum> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Stanford Mausoleum**, located in the Northwest of the [Stanford University](:Stanford_University) campus in the [Stanford University Arboretum](:Stanford_University_Arboretum), holds the remains of the university's namesake [Leland Stanford, Jr.](:Leland_Stanford%2C_Jr%2E) and his parents [Leland](:Leland_Stanford) and [Jane Stanford](:Jane_Stanford).Once per year, the [mausoleum](:Mausoleum) is opened to the public and a wreath laid (usually in October during the reunion weekend) as part of the annual Founders' Day activities."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
