<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Aviation_Martyrs'_Monument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Aviation Martyrs' Monument** (Template:Lang-tr or formerly *Tayyare Şehitleri Abidesi*), located in [Fatih](:Fatih) district of [Istanbul](:Istanbul), [Turkey](:Turkey), is a [memorial](:Memorial) dedicated to the first soldiers of the [Ottoman Airforce](:Ottoman_Airforce) to be killed in flight accidents. In Turkey, one use of the term \"martyr\" is as an honorific for people killed in action during war.The monument was commissioned right after the consecutive crash of two [monoplanes](:Monoplane) in [Palestine](:Palestine_%28region%29), killing three of the four military aviators who were on an [expedition flight](:Aviation_Squadrons_%28Ottoman_Empire)#Constantinople-to-Cairo_flight) from Istanbul to [Alexandria](:Alexandria) in early 1914. The monument, in form of a [column](:Column), was inaugurated in 1916. A military memorial ceremony is held in front of the monument every year on Martyrs' Day."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
