<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Junagadh> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Junagadh** () is the headquarters of [Junagadh district](:Junagadh_district) in the [Indian state](:States_and_territories_of_India) of [Gujarat](:Gujarat). Located at the foot of the [Girnar hills](:Girnar), 355 kilometres (221 mi) southwest of [Ahmedabad](:Ahmedabad) and [Gandhinagar](:Gandhinagar) (the state capital), it is the seventh largest city in the state.Literally translated, Junagadh means \"Old Fort\".After a brief struggle between India and Pakistan, Junagadh voted to join India in a plebiscite held on 20 February 1948. It was a part of Saurashtra state and later Bombay state. In 1960, in consequence of the Maha Gujarat movement, it became part of the newly formed Gujarat state."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
