<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russell_Alger_Memorial_Fountain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Russell Alger Memorial Fountain is a Detroit, Michigan fountain, one of the \"most successful collaborations\" created by the sculptor, Daniel Chester French and architect Henry Bacon. The bronze statue was cast by the Gorham Manufacturing Company. It is located in Grand Circus Park and was dedicated on July 27, 1921."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ion_Mincu> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Ion Mincu (Romanian pronunciation: [iˈon ˈmiŋku]; December 20, 1852 – December 6, 1912 in Bucharest) was a Romanian architect known for having a leading role in the development of the Romanian Revival style. Most of his projects are located in Bucharest, including his main works, the Palace of Justice, the , and the Central Girls' School."@en .
