<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Martqopi_monastery> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Martqopi monastery of the Deity** ([Georgian](:Georgian_language): მარტყოფის ღვთაების მონასტერი, [romanized](:Romanization_of_Georgian): mart'q'opis ghvtaebis monast'eri) is a [Georgian Orthodox](:Georgian_Orthodox) monastery near the village of [Martqopi](:Martqopi), some 25 km east of [Tbilisi](:Tbilisi), the capital of [Georgia](:Georgia_%28country%29). The history of the monastery dates back to [stylite](:Stylite) practices in the 6th century and is linked by historical tradition with St. Anton, one of the [Thirteen Assyrian Fathers](:Thirteen_Assyrian_Fathers). Most of the monastery's extant structures are from the 17th to the 19th century. The monastery is inscribed on the list of the [Immovable Cultural Monuments of National Significance](:Immovable_Cultural_Monuments_of_National_Significance) of Georgia."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
