<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sytin's_house_in_Sytinsky_lane> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Sytin's house in Sytinsky lane** (Template:Lang-ru is a wooden building in the center of [Moscow](:Moscow) (Sytinsky lane, house 5, building 5). A unique example of the construction of the city before the fire of 1812, it is the main house of the city manor of the noble family Sytinykh. The house was built in 1804 in the [classicism](:Classicism) style. It has the status of an object of cultural heritage of federal significance."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
