<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brest,_Belarus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Brest (Belarusian: Брэст / Берасьце, Bieraście, pronounced [brɛs̪t̪]; Russian: Брест, pronounced [brʲes̪t̪]; Lithuanian: Brasta; Polish: Brześć; Yiddish: בריסק, romanized: Brisk), formerly Brest-Litovsk (Russian: Брест-Литовск, lit. 'Lithuanian Brest'; Belarusian: Берасце Літоўскі (Берасце), romanized: Berastze Litouski (Berastze); Lithuanian: Lietuvos Brasta; Polish: Brześć Litewski, Yiddish: בריסק דליטא), Brest-on-the-Bug (Polish: Brześć nad Bugiem), is a city (population 350,616 in 2019) in Belarus at the border with Poland opposite the Polish city of Terespol, where the Bug and Mukhavets rivers meet, making it a border town. It is the capital city of the Brest Region."@en .
