<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Madrid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Madrid** ( [*mə-DRID*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key), Template:IPA-es is the capital and most populous city of [Spain](:Spain). The city has almost 3.4 million inhabitants and a [metropolitan area](:Madrid_metropolitan_area) population of approximately 6.7 million. It is the [second-largest city](:Largest_cities_of_the_European_Union_by_population_within_city_limits) in the [European Union](:European_Union) (EU), and its [monocentric](https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monocentric) [metropolitan area](:Madrid_metropolitan_area) is the [third-largest](:List_of_metropolitan_areas_in_Europe_by_population) in the EU. The municipality covers 604.3 km2 (233.3 sq mi) geographical area.Madrid lies on the [River Manzanares](:Manzanares_%28river%29) in the central part of the [Iberian Peninsula](:Iberian_Peninsula). Capital city of both Spain (almost without interruption since 1561) and the surrounding [autonomous community of Madrid](:Community_of_Madrid) (since 1983), it is also the political, economic and cultural centre of the country. The city is situated on an elevated plain about 300 km (190 mi) from the closest seaside location. The [climate of Madrid](:Climate_of_Madrid) features hot summers and cool winters.The Madrid urban agglomeration has the [second-largest GDP](:List_of_cities_by_GDP) in the [European Union](:European_Union) and its influence in [politics](:Politics), [education](:Education), [entertainment](:Entertainment), [environment](:Built_environment), [media](:Mass_media), [fashion](:Fashion), [science](:Science), [culture](:Culture), and the [arts](:Arts) all contribute to its status as one of the world's major [global cities](:Global_city). Due to its [economic output](:Output_%28economics%29), high [standard of living](:Standard_of_living), and market size, Madrid is considered the major financial centre and the leading economic hub of the Iberian Peninsula and of [Southern Europe](:Southern_Europe). The metropolitan area hosts major Spanish companies such as [Telefónica](:Telef%C3%B3nica), [Iberia](:Iberia_%28airline%29), [BBVA](:BBVA) and [FCC](:Fomento_de_Construcciones_y_Contratas). It concentrates the bulk of banking operations in the country and it is the Spanish-speaking city generating the largest amount of webpages.Madrid houses the headquarters of the [UN](:United_Nations)'s [World Tourism Organization](:World_Tourism_Organization) (UNWTO), the [Ibero-American General Secretariat](:Ibero-American_General_Secretariat) (SEGIB), the [Organization of Ibero-American States](:Organization_of_Ibero-American_States) (OEI), and the [Public Interest Oversight Board](:Public_Interest_Oversight_Board) (PIOB). It also hosts major international regulators and promoters of the Spanish language: the Standing Committee of the Association of Spanish Language Academies, headquarters of the [Royal Spanish Academy](:Royal_Spanish_Academy) (RAE), the [Instituto Cervantes](:Instituto_Cervantes) and the Foundation of Emerging Spanish ([Fundéu](:Fund%C3%A9u)RAE). Madrid organises fairs such as FITUR, ARCO, [SIMO TCI](:SIMO_TCI) and the [Madrid Fashion Week](:Madrid_Fashion_Week). Madrid is home to two world-famous [football](:Association_football) clubs, [Real Madrid](:Real_Madrid) and [Atlético Madrid](:Atl%C3%A9tico_Madrid).While Madrid possesses modern infrastructure, it has preserved the look and feel of many of its historic neighbourhoods and streets. Its landmarks include the [Plaza Mayor](:Plaza_Mayor%2C_Madrid), the [Royal Palace of Madrid](:Royal_Palace_of_Madrid); the [Royal Theatre](:Teatro_Real) with its restored 1850 Opera House; the [Buen Retiro Park](:Buen_Retiro_Park), founded in 1631; the 19th-century [National Library](:Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Espa%C3%B1a) building (founded in 1712) containing some of Spain's historical archives; many national museums, and the [Golden Triangle of Art](:Golden_Triangle_of_Art), located along the [Paseo del Prado](:Paseo_del_Prado) and comprising three art museums: [Prado Museum](:Museo_del_Prado), the [Reina Sofía Museum](:Museo_Nacional_Centro_de_Arte_Reina_Sof%C3%ADa), a museum of [modern art](:Modern_art), and the [Thyssen-Bornemisza Museum](:Thyssen-Bornemisza_Museum), which complements the holdings of the other two museums. [Cibeles Palace and Fountain](:Plaza_de_Cibeles) has become one of the monument symbols of the city. The mayor is [José Luis Martínez-Almeida](:Jos%C3%A9_Luis_Mart%C3%ADnez-Almeida) from the [People's Party](:People%27s_Party_%28Spain%29)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
