<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Archdiocesan_Marian_Shrine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Archdiocesan Marian Shrine**, formerly known as the **Milwaukee Fatima Shrine** and the **National Shrine to Our Lady of Fatima**, is of the [Roman Catholic Church](:Roman_Catholic_Church) and a [shrine to the Virgin Mary](:Shrines_to_the_Virgin_Mary). It is operated by the [Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Milwaukee](:Roman_Catholic_Archdiocese_of_Milwaukee), which acquired the property from the [Dominican Sisters of the Perpetual Rosary](:Dominican_Nuns_of_the_Perpetual_Rosary). It is located in [Milwaukee](:Milwaukee), [Wisconsin](:Wisconsin). The shrine was dedicated on April 26, 1948. The shrine also has a small indoor chapel and stone representations of the 15 mysteries of the [rosary](:Rosary)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
