<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Monument_to_Álvaro_de_Bazán_(Madrid)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Monument to Álvaro de Bazán** is an instance of public art in [Madrid](:Madrid), Spain. Located at the [Plaza de la Villa](:Plaza_de_la_Villa), it consists of a bronze sculpture designed by [Mariano Benlliure](:Mariano_Benlliure) representing [Álvaro de Bazán](:%C3%81lvaro_de_Baz%C3%A1n)—a noted 16th century Admiral of the [Spanish Navy](:Spanish_Navy) once described by [Cervantes](:Cervantes) as \"father of soldiers, lightning of war, fortunate and never defeated captain\"— put on top of a stone pedestal."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
