<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bazaar> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A bazaar (Persian: بازار) or souk (Arabic: سوق, romanized: sūq; also transliterated as souq) is a marketplace consisting of multiple small stalls or shops, especially in the Middle East, Northeast Africa, and India. However temporary open markets elsewhere, such as in the West might also designate themselves to be bazaars. The ones in the Middle East were traditionally located in vaulted or covered streets that had doors on each end and served as a city's central marketplace. Street markets are the European and North American equivalents."@en .
