<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bochorma_fortress> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Bochorma fortress** ([Georgian](:Georgian_language): ბოჭორმის ციხე, [romanized](:Romanization_of_Georgian): boch'ormis tsikhe) is a medieval architectural complex in eastern [Georgia](:Georgia_%28country%29), located in the [Tianeti Municipality](:Tianeti_Municipality) in the [region](:Mkhare) of [Mtskheta-Mtianeti](:Mtskheta-Mtianeti). Historically it was part of [principality of Kakheti](:First_Kingdom_of_Kakheti). Situated on a high mount on the [Iori River](:Iori_River), the complex consists of a castle and a domed [dodecagonal](:Dodecagon) church, both dated to the 10th century, as well as another small [hall church](:Hall_church), and some other accessory structures. All structures within the complex are half-ruined or significantly damaged. They are all inscribed on the list of the [Immovable Cultural Monuments of National Significance](:Immovable_Cultural_Monuments_of_National_Significance)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
