<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Walter_Seymour_Allward> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Walter Seymour Allward, CMG RCA (18 November 1874 – 24 April 1955) was a Canadian monumental sculptor best known for the Canadian National Vimy Memorial. Featuring expressive classical figures within modern compositions, Allward's monuments evoke themes of memory, sacrifice, and redemption. He has been widely praised for his \"original sense of spatial composition, his mastery of the classical form and his brilliant craftsmanship\"."@en .
