<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Millennium_Monument_of_Brest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Brest Millennium Monument** (2009) - was designed by the Belarusian architect [Alexei Andreyuk](:Alexei_Andreyuk) and sculptor Alexei Pavluchuk to commemorate the millennium of [Brest, Belarus](:Brest%2C_Belarus). It was erected in 2009 at the intersection of Sovietskaya Street and Gogol Street in Brest. The project was financed by the state budget and public donations.The monument presents a group of bronze statues. The angel of mercy with a cross is standing at the top of a granite column. 3 statues remember the remarkable historic personalities that are associated with Brest:[Vladimir Vasilkovich](:Vladimir_Vasilkovich), who put up a tower in the castle of the town in the 13th century,[Vytautas](:Vytautas) the grand duke of [Grand Duchy of Lithuania](:Grand_Duchy_of_Lithuania),[Mikołaj \"the Black\" Radziwiłł](:Miko%C5%82aj_%22the_Black%22_Radziwi%C5%82%C5%82) in whose printing shop the first Belarusian book was printed,3 more statues represent abstract images: warrior, mother, chronicler (who wrote apparently the [Primary Chronicle](:Primary_Chronicle%29).The total height is 15.1 m,the height of the angel is 3.8 m,the height of the 6 statues is 3m.the diameter of the base is 8.6 m.In April 2011 a belt of high reliefs appeared around the monument. It depicts history-making episodes of [Brest](:Brest%2C_Belarus).  "^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
