<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Torre_da_TV_Bandeirantes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Maria Helena Mendes de Barros Saad Tower**, more commonly known as **Torre da TV Bandeirantes**, or **Torre da Band**, is a television and radio [lattice tower](:Lattice_tower) located in the district of Consolação, near the [Avenida Paulista](:Avenida_Paulista) in [São Paulo](:S%C3%A3o_Paulo), Brazil. Owned by the Brazilian media company [Grupo Bandeirantes de Comunicação](:Grupo_Bandeirantes_de_Comunica%C3%A7%C3%A3o), the tower is 212 m (696 ft) high, making it the tallest tower in São Paulo and one of the tallest towers in Latin America. Its name is in honor of the wife of the founder of Rede Bandeirantes, João Saad."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
