<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spire_of_Notre-Dame_de_Paris> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **spire of Notre-Dame de Paris** was located above the cross-section of the cathedral's [transept](:Transept). [Notre-Dame de Paris](:Notre-Dame_de_Paris) has had two timber [spires](:Spire), known as [flèches](:Fl%C3%A8che_%28architecture%29). The first was built between 1220 and 1230. It eventually became so damaged that it was removed in the late 18th century. The second was put into place by the French architect [Eugène Viollet-le-Duc](:Eug%C3%A8ne_Viollet-le-Duc) in 1859, and destroyed in [a major fire](:Notre-Dame_de_Paris_fire) on 15 April 2019."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
