<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lahovari_House> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Lahovari House** (Template:Lang-ro is a house in the [sector 2](:Sector_2_%28Bucharest%29) of [Bucharest](:Bucharest), built by [Ion Mincu](:Ion_Mincu) between 1884 and 1886, at the request of [Iacob Lahovary](:Iacob_Lahovary) (1846–1907), general and politician, Minister of Foreign Affairs, Minister of War and Chief of the General Staff. The building is considered to be the first significant [Romanian Revival](:Romanian_Revival_architecture) style building in the history of Romanian architecture. one of Ion Mincu's early works, it is considered to be emblematic of his style. The building was used as a home for most of its life; since 2003 it has been used by the Maternity Department of the Cantacuzino Hospital. It is classified as a [historic monument](:Monument_istoric)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
