<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lviv> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Lviv (/ləˈviːv, ləˈviːf/ lə-VEEV, lə-VEEF; Ukrainian: Львів [lʲwiu̯]; Polish: Lwów [lvuf]; Russian: Львов, romanized: Lvov [lʲvof]; German: Lemberg; see also ) is the largest city in Western Ukraine, and the sixth-largest in Ukraine, with a population of 717,510 (2021 est.) Lviv is one of the main cultural centres of Ukraine. It was named in honour of Leo, the eldest son of Daniel, King of Ruthenia."@en .
