<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Malakpet> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Malakpet** is one of the suburbs in the old city area of [Hyderabad](:Hyderabad), Telangana, India. It is famous for TV tower which was built by Teegala Sree Ramulu. This is further divided into two parts, Old Malakpet and New Malakpet and is traditionally considered part of old city. This circle (6) comes under Charminar Zone of [Greater Hyderabad Municipal Corporation](:Greater_Hyderabad_Municipal_Corporation). There are seven wards in this circle namely [Saidabad](:Saidabad) (24), [Moosrambagh](:Moosarambagh) (25), Old Malakpet (26), Akberbagh (27), [Azampura](:Azampura) (28), Chawani (29) and [Dabeerpura](:Dabirpura) (30).[Ahmed bin Abdullah Balala](:Ahmed_bin_Abdullah_Balala) of the [All India Majlis-e-Ittehadul Muslimeen](:All_India_Majlis-e-Ittehadul_Muslimeen) party was elected MLA of the [Malakpet Assembly constituency](:Malakpet_Assembly_constituency) for the third time in 2018."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
