<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Erode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Erode** (Template:IPA-ta is a city in the Indian state of [Tamil Nadu](:Tamil_Nadu). Erode is the seventh largest urban agglomeration in the state, after [Chennai](:Chennai), [Coimbatore](:Coimbatore), [Madurai](:Madurai), [Tiruchirapalli](:Tiruchirapalli), [Tiruppur](:Tiruppur) and [Salem](:Salem%2C_Tamil_Nadu). It is also the administrative headquarters of the [Erode district](:Erode_district). Administered by a [city municipal corporation](:Erode_Municipal_Corporation) since 2008, Erode is a part of [Erode Lok Sabha constituency](:Erode_%28Lok_Sabha_constituency%29) that elects its [member of parliament](:Member_of_Parliament%2C_Lok_Sabha). Located on the banks of [River Kaveri](:River_Kaveri), it is situated centrally on South Indian [Peninsula](:Peninsula), about 400 kilometres (249 mi) southwest of its state capital [Chennai](:Chennai), 250 kilometres (155 mi) south of [Bengaluru](:Bengaluru), 100 kilometres (62 mi) east of [Coimbatore](:Coimbatore) and 275 kilometres (171 mi) east of [Kochi](:Kochi). Erode is an agricultural, textile and a [BPO](:Business_process_outsourcing_to_India) hub and among the largest producers of [turmeric](:Turmeric), hand-loom and knitwear, and food products."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
