<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chapultepec> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Chapultepec, more commonly called the \"Bosque de Chapultepec\" (Chapultepec Forest) in Mexico City, is one of the largest city parks in Mexico, measuring in total just over 686 hectares (1,695 acres). Centered on a rock formation called Chapultepec Hill, one of the park's main functions is as an ecological space in Greater Mexico City. It is considered the first and most important of Mexico City's \"lungs\"."@en .
