<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ohel_(Chabad-Lubavitch)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In the [Chabad-Lubavitch](:Chabad) Jewish movement, the **Ohel** (Template:Lang-he is an *[ohel](:Ohel_%28grave%29)* (Jewish monumental tomb) in New York City at which the Rabbi [Menachem Mendel Schneerson](:Menachem_Mendel_Schneerson), and his father-in-law, Rabbi [Yosef Yitzchok Schneersohn](:Yosef_Yitzchok_Schneersohn), (the two most recent [rebbes](:Rebbe) of the Chabad-Lubavitch dynasty) are buried. The Ohel is visited by thousands of Jews and non-Jews each year. Approximately 50,000 people made a pilgrimage in 2014 on the anniversary of Schneerson's death."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
