<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lagurka> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Kala church of Saints Cyricus and Julitta** ([Georgian](:Georgian_language): კალას წმინდა კვირიკესა და ივლიტას სახელობის ეკლესია, [romanized](:Romanization_of_Georgian): k'alas ts'minda k'virik'esa da ivlit'as sakhelobis ek'lesia), locally known as **Lagurka** (ლაგურკა), is a medieval church in the [Mestia Municipality](:Mestia_Municipality) in [Georgia](:Georgia_%28country%29)'s [region](:Mkhare) of [Samegrelo-Zemo Svaneti](:Samegrelo-Zemo_Svaneti). The area is part of the highland historical and cultural region of [Upper Svaneti](:Upper_Svaneti) where Lagurka is regarded as the principal Christian shrine, its designation deriving from the name of Cyricus in the local [Svan language](:Svan_language). It is a [hall church](:Hall_church), adorned with frescoes painted by Tevdore in 1111/1112, one of the high points of medieval Georgian monumental art. The church is inscribed on the list of the [Immovable Cultural Monuments of National Significance](:Immovable_Cultural_Monuments_of_National_Significance) of Georgia."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
