<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Monument_Indië-Nederland> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Monument Indië-Nederland** is located near the Olympiaplein in the southern part of [Amsterdam](:Amsterdam). The monument was originally a memorial for General [J. B. van Heutsz](:J%2E_B%2E_van_Heutsz), who was the commandant of the Royal Netherlands East Indies Army and is also known for conquering [Aceh](:Aceh) for the [Kingdom of the Netherlands](:Kingdom_of_the_Netherlands) in 1903 following the [Aceh War](:Aceh_War). Because of political pressure the name was in 2004 changed to Monument Indië-Nederland."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
