<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Husainabad_Clock_Tower> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Husainabad Clock Tower is a clock tower located in the Lucknow city of India. It was constructed in 1881 by Hussainabad Trust to mark the arrival of Sir George Couper, the first lieutenant governor of the United Province of Avadh. It was built at a cost of Rs. 1.75 lakhs."@en .
