<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Aviation_Martyrs'_Monument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Aviation Martyrs' Monument (Turkish: Hava Şehitleri Anıtı or formerly Tayyare Şehitleri Abidesi), located in Fatih district of Istanbul, Turkey, is a memorial dedicated to the first soldiers of the Ottoman Airforce to be killed in flight accidents. In Turkey, one use of the term \"martyr\" is as an honorific for people killed in action during war."@en .
